# Die for real, then look at the gravestone (bd inc-r6z, bd inc-nx0z).
#
#   INCURSION_GRAVESTONE_PROBE=1 INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/gates/Options.Dat \
#   INCURSION_LOAD=tools/fixtures/chars/orc-barbarian-seed1-gate.sav \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/gravestone.keys 1
#
# src/GravestoneProbe.cpp deals lethal damage after the first completed turn, which the 's' below spends.
# The pinned gate settings run with OPT_NODEATH on, so the killing blow asks
# "You die... Die? [yn]" (src/Fight.cpp) and the 'y' below answers it. After
# Player::Death() runs, src/Main.cpp waits for ENTER and then calls
# Player::Gravestone(), which draws the stone before it asks for anything. So
# the screen dumped below IS the death screen a player sees. 'q' is what the
# gravestone's own prompt ("[dvmqs]") accepts for Quit; @quit would not be
# read there.

s
y*3
ENTER

@dump:gravestone

q
